Adds an engine-owned scroll signal to CodeView: subscribeToScroll listeners get
{ engineOwned } saying whether a scroll landed where the view's own scroll
correction (applyScrollFix) put it. Omnigent's rich diff review uses it to keep
a reader's place when the width changes, without guessing ownership by time.

Upstream issue: drafted, not yet filed ("CodeView scroll listeners can't tell the
view's own scroll corrections from anyone else's"). Drop this patch once
@pierre/diffs ships an equivalent signal. See patches/README.md.

Also turns a diff row with no line on either side into a failure for that file: the
renderer throws a DiffMissingRowError that says which side was short, and FileDiff
hands it to an onRenderError option (passed through CodeView) instead of printing the
error and its stack into the file. Omnigent's review shows a note for that file and
records a diagnostic. See patches/README.md.

